 ## Background
-Pre-integration was introduced by Roettger and Ertl [S2, unofficial]. It addresses the problem that the discrete approximation of the volume rendering integral converges to correct results only for high sampling rates [S2, unofficial]. The technique pre-computes the integral of the opacity and color transfer functions for all possible pairs of scalar values at the boundaries of a slab [S2, unofficial]. It is often applied in conjunction with shading models, such as the Phong model, to pre-integrate ambient, diffuse, and specular lighting parameters [S2, unofficial].
+Pre-integration was introduced by Roettger and Ertl [S2, unofficial]. It addresses the problem that the discrete approximation of the volume rendering integral converges to correct results only for high sampling rates [S2, unofficial]. The technique pre-computes the integral of the opacity or color transfer function for each combination of scalar values and stores it in a 2D lookup table for constant sampling distance [S2, unofficial]. It is often applied in conjunction with shading models, such as the Phong model, to pre-integrate ambient, diffuse, and specular lighting parameters [S2, unofficial].
 
